dialect protocol stdio.zip.diff
; `ZipDiff::encode_op` is `serde_json::to_vec` of the exact same shape as the text-facet grammar
; (`../📝️text/📖️component.grammar.semio`) — the "binary" op-wire form is UTF-8 JSON bytes, not a
; packed binary layout (no magic/length-prefix framing exists at this facet; the caller already
; knows the byte-slice boundary). Documented here rather than hidden behind a placeholder.
payload = utf8-bytes-of(diff-line) ; `diff-line` is defined by the sibling text grammar; the
                                    ; binary op is exactly its UTF-8 byte encoding, no framing.
